---
import MakerLayout from '../../layouts/MakerLayout.astro';
import demand from '../../data/demand.json';
import seoOpportunities from '../../data/seo-opportunities.json';
const top = demand.opportunities.slice(0, 6);
const trends = demand.globalTrends?.slice(0, 20) || [];
const catalog = demand.catalogDiscovery || [];
---
<MakerLayout title="Global Search & Demand Radar — PARADOX Makers" description="A transparent multi-source demand radar using public aggregate trend, media, Wikimedia, developer and API-catalog signals to surface useful free generators.">
  <main class="maker-main">
    <section class="maker-hero compact-hero">
      <div>
        <div class="maker-kicker">GLOBAL DEMAND INTELLIGENCE</div>
        <h1>See what is moving.<br/><em>Serve a real job.</em></h1>
        <p>PARADOX samples public aggregate signals across countries, then maps them to actual tools. It is designed to adapt discovery automatically without buying traffic or tracking individual people.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="maker-proof">
        <div class="proof-tile"><strong>REFRESHED</strong><span>{demand.refreshedAt}</span></div>
        <div class="proof-tile"><strong>SEARCH SIGNALS</strong><span>{demand.sourceHealth?.googleTrends?.rows || 0} trend rows</span></div>
        <div class="proof-tile"><strong>NO PRIVATE DATA</strong><span>Public aggregate sources only.</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="maker-section">
      <div class="maker-section-head"><div><div class="maker-label">LIVE SIGNAL SAMPLE</div><h2>Trending across<br/>multiple markets.</h2></div><p>Google Trends exposes aggregate Trending Now data for many countries/regions. These rows are signals for discovery, not promises of exact search volume or rankings.</p></div>
      <div class="maker-tools">
        {trends.map((item, index) => <a class="maker-card" href="/use-cases/"><div><div class="maker-card-top"><div class="maker-icon">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</div><span>{item.geo}</span></div><h2>{item.query}</h2><p>{item.traffic || 'Trending'} · {item.pubDate || 'current public signal'}</p></div><div class="maker-open">See useful matches →</div></a>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="maker-section">
      <div class="maker-section-head"><div><div class="maker-label">TOOL FIT</div><h2>Attention becomes<br/><em>action.</em></h2></div><p>Each score is a relative internal ranking. It combines trend matches with public media attention and is used to decide which existing tool gets more visibility.</p></div>
      <div class="maker-tools">
        {top.map((item, index) => <a class="maker-card" href={item.route}><div><div class="maker-card-top"><div class="maker-icon">0{index+1}</div><span>score {item.score}</span></div><h2>{item.label}</h2><p>{item.trendMatches?.length || 0} matching trend signals · {item.mediaSignal || 0} media signal units</p></div><div class="maker-open">Use this tool →</div></a>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="maker-section">
      <div class="maker-section-head"><div><div class="maker-label">AUTOMATIC SEO LAYER</div><h2>{seoOpportunities.length} focused pages,<br/>only when earned.</h2></div><p>The engine can turn a strong trend/tool match into a focused use-case page. It caps the count and requires a real underlying generator to keep these pages useful instead of creating keyword-only doorway pages.</p></div>
      <div class="maker-guide-grid">{seoOpportunities.slice(0,8).map(item => <a class="maker-guide" href={`/use-cases/${item.slug}/`}><strong>{item.title}</strong><br/>{item.description}</a>)}</div>
    </section>

    <section class="maker-section">
      <div class="maker-section-head"><div><div class="maker-label">API DISCOVERY</div><h2>Two large API catalogs<br/>feed the scout.</h2></div><p>The public-apis and Awesome-APIs repositories are treated as discovery registries. The engine scans them for relevant public sources; it does not blindly call thousands of third-party APIs.</p></div>
      <div class="maker-guide-grid">{catalog.map(source => <article class="maker-guide"><strong>{source.name}</strong><br/>{source.scanned ? `Scanned ${source.totalRelevant} relevant catalog entries.` : 'Waiting for the next successful refresh.'}</article>)}</div>
    </section>

    <section class="maker-section">
      <article class="maker-why">
        <div class="maker-label">WHY THIS IS DIFFERENT</div>
        <h1>A traffic system, not an ad campaign.</h1>
        <p>The goal is to compound organic discovery: watch aggregate demand, connect it to a real task, publish only useful pages, update the sitemap during every build, and keep the generators immediately usable.</p>
        <p>That can increase the probability of organic discovery, but no system can honestly guarantee immediate traffic, rankings, AdSense approval or revenue. Search engines decide what they index and rank.</p>
        <p><a href="/">Back to PARADOX Makers →</a></p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</MakerLayout>
